From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:06:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: prepare to render buffers a Wayland client hands
 over

Kodi can host Wayland clients and show their surfaces through its
video renderers. For that, the build looks for wayland-server,
wayland-scanner and the protocol definitions, taking linux-dmabuf from
unstable/ where wayland-protocols has no stable/ copy yet; the DRM
PRIME renderers accept DRM PRIME buffers whatever the decoder setting
says, as these buffers come from no decoder; and CVideoBufferDMA copes
with a factory that has no buffer object to export.

A DRM PRIME buffer may prefer a display plane, and the plane renderer
then takes it whatever the setting for DRM PRIME video picks, with the
GLES renderer behind it for formats no plane shows. A video layer
bridge derived from CVideoLayerBridgeDRMPRIME creates framebuffers for
buffers of its own with the same conversion from a buffer's
descriptor.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
